<title>USA: U.S. 2-year note auction high yield 5.874 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. 2-year note auction high yield 5.874 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Treasury said its Dutch bidding auction of 2-year notes produced these results:</p>
<p>			 2-YEAR NOTES DUE DEC 31, 1998</p>
<p>			     $18.250 BILLION AUCTION</p>
<p>	     YIELD			  PRICE	COUPON</p>
<p> HIGH	5.874    Awarded At	99.769	5.750</p>
<p> MEDIAN    5.850    High Yield	NOT GIVEN  Percent</p>
<p> LOW	 5.800    16 Percent	NOT GIVEN</p>
<p>	   Cover - (Bids Over Amount Sold)    =  2.23 Times</p>
<p> U.S. TREASURY (GOVERNMENT DEBT)		 MATURITY 31.Dec.98</p>
<p> MATURITY/TYPE    2-YEAR NOTES		   PAY DATE 31.Dec.96</p>
<p> TYPE OF DEBT     STRAIGHT			 LAUNCHED 18.Dec.96</p>
<p> ISSUED/ACCEPTED  18.250 BLN USD		 CUSIP    9128272D3</p>
<p> BIDS SUBMITTED   40.634			   COUNTRY	  USA</p>
<p> NONCOMPETITIVE    1.340				DUTCH AUCTION</p>
<p> NY FED DISTRICT    N.A.			   COUPON	 5.750</p>
<p> FOREIGN INSTITN   1.450			   PRICE	 99.769</p>
<p> BIDDING RANGE    5.800-5.874 PCT		YIELD-HIGH   5.874</p>
<p> KEY (HIGH) YIELD UP FROM 5.622 PCT AT AUCTION ON 19.NOV.96</p>
<p> KEY (HIGH) YIELD HIGHEST SINCE 5.930 PCT AT AUCTION 22.OCT.96</p>
</text>
